fragment_downloaded_cb({"url":"Reference-manual_elementary_int.html#arguments","fragment":"Arguments\nThe method int.to_string() accepts the following positional arguments:\n\nFinally, int.to_string()\naccepts the following keyword arguments:\n\n\n    \n      \n        Name\n        Type\n        Description\n        Tags\n      \n    \n    \n      \n        fill\n        int\n        \n        \nLeft fill the string with zeros until it reaches the length\nspecified by this argument. A leading negative sign counts towards\nthe length, and is handled by inserting the padding after the -\ncharacter rather than before. The original string is returned if the\nvalue provided is less than or equal to the former's length.\n  \n        \n\n  [optional]\n  \n  \n      \n    \n  \n\n    \n      \n        Name\n        Type\n        Description\n        Tags\n      \n    \n    \n      \n        format\n        str\n        \n        \nHow to format the number; can be one of 'dec' (decimal), 'hex'\n(hexadecimal), 'oct' (octal), or 'bin' (binary).\nFor formats other than 'dec', the string will be appropriately prefixed\n(e.g., for 'hex', the string will begin with '0x', etc.)\n  \n        \n\n  (since 1.12.0)\n  default =\n  'dec'\n  \n  \n      \n    \n  \n"});